{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>If another.</b> Whether she be an Israelite daughter who was sold or not sold." "<b>Her food.</b> Her sustenance; he must provide her שארה, which is her meat." "<b>And her conjugal duty.</b> Some say her dwelling, and similar to it according to their view: וענה איים (Isaiah 13:22), וענתה שמה (Hosea 2:17). In my view, וענה איים is as it sounds, like וענית ואמרת (Deuteronomy 26:5) by way of parable, for there it is written ושעיר על רעהו יקרא (Isaiah 34:14). Also, וענתה שמה (Hosea 2:17) is to be sung, like ענו לה' בתודה (Psalms 147:7). And he explained ועונתה as the time of lying together, which is the time of love, for the word עת in the absence of נו\"ן is like אמת; therefore the ת\"ו receives a dagesh, as in והנה עִתֵּךְ (Ezekiel 16:8), or עתו like אַמִתּוֹ, likewise עַתָּה. And behold, עונתה is derived from עת, and now this is that time."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:49.593684658Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}